WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.460
A tree keeps adding roots, branches and leaves for as long as it lives.

2
00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.500
Take the root of a flowering plant.

3
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:18.320
It gets longer. Does it make more cells, or do its cells get longer?

4
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:24.380
Behind the tip, under a protective root cap, you can see three zones.

5
00:00:25.433 --> 00:00:28.793
In the zone of division, small cells divide.

6
00:00:29.693 --> 00:00:35.413
In the zone of elongation, they stop dividing and lengthen many times over, as water

7
00:00:35.413 --> 00:00:36.533
fills their vacuoles.

8
00:00:37.353 --> 00:00:42.513
In the zone of maturation, they become their final types, and root hairs appear on

9
00:00:42.513 --> 00:00:43.513
the epidermis.

10
00:00:43.983 --> 00:00:46.463
So growth has two parts.

11
00:00:47.343 --> 00:00:48.883
Division makes the cells.

12
00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:51.823
Elongation sets their length.

13
00:00:53.003 --> 00:00:57.243
Assume the root is at steady state, with every cell file alike.

14
00:00:58.243 --> 00:01:04.283
Then root growth rate equals the rate of new cells per file, times the final cell

15
00:01:04.283 --> 00:01:07.783
length. The numbers that follow are illustrative.

16
00:01:08.263 --> 00:01:09.743
They are not from a measured species.

17
00:01:10.733 --> 00:01:13.373
Take one file of cells.

18
00:01:14.173 --> 00:01:17.633
It delivers one new cell per hour from the meristem.

19
00:01:18.553 --> 00:01:25.373
Each cell leaves the meristem 15 micrometers long, and matures at 300 micrometers.

20
00:01:26.433 --> 00:01:32.473
One cell per hour times 300 micrometers is 300 micrometers per hour.

21
00:01:33.253 --> 00:01:37.313
Over 24 hours, that is 7.2 millimeters per day.

22
00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:42.487
Now block elongation, and leave division alone.

23
00:01:43.407 --> 00:01:46.387
Division still delivers one new cell per hour.

24
00:01:46.987 --> 00:01:49.827
But the cells stay 15 micrometers long.

25
00:01:50.747 --> 00:01:54.167
One times 15 is 15 micrometers per hour.

26
00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:59.747
That is 0.36 millimeters per day, one twentieth of normal.

27
00:02:00.507 --> 00:02:03.107
So elongation supplies most of the length.

28
00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:08.490
Instead, halve division, and keep elongation normal.

29
00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:15.650
Half a cell per hour times 300 micrometers is 150 micrometers per hour.

30
00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:20.430
That is 3.6 millimeters per day, half of normal.

31
00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:24.950
A change in growth can come from either part, or from both.

32
00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:31.870
Keep the rule. Root growth rate equals new cells per hour times final cell length.
